body_md:
こんにちは、しぃちゃんだよ！今日は無料枠で試せるようになった、嬉しいニュースだよ！

## なにが発表されたの？

Cloudflare の Changelog で、Email Service の Email Sending が Workers Free プランで使えるようになったと発表されたよ！アカウントの認証済み宛先アドレスへの送信が対象なの。

## これで何が変わるの？

送信ドメインのオンボーディングが、有料プランなしでできるようになったよ。開発やテストの間は認証済み宛先へ無料で送って、本番で任意の宛先に送るときに Workers Paid プランへ上がれるんだよ。Workers バインディング、REST API、SMTP を使って、チームへのアラート、レポート、通知を送れるよ！

## 深く潜ってみよう

認証済み宛先アドレスへの送信は、すべてのプランで無料だよ。月間のクォータにも、1 日あたりの送信上限にも数えられないの。

Workers バインディングの例は、こんな感じだよ。認証済みでない宛先に送ると、E_RECIPIENT_PLAN_RESTRICTED というエラーコードが返るよ。

```js
export default {
  async fetch(request, env) {
    try {
      await env.EMAIL.send({
        from: "alerts@yourdomain.com",
        to: "oncall@example.com", // A verified destination address
        subject: "Disk usage above 90%",
        text: "Disk usage on db-1 is above 90%.",
      });
    } catch (error) {
      if (error.code === "E_RECIPIENT_PLAN_RESTRICTED") {
        return new Response("Recipient is not a verified destination address", {
          status: 403,
        });
      }
      throw error;
    }
    return new Response("Alert sent");
  },
};
```

### 集計の扱いが変わるよ

これまで、認証済み宛先への送信は Email Routing の機能で、Email Routing のトラフィックとして記録されていたよ。今回、この機能が Email Sending に移ったの。

- 送信ドメインから認証済み宛先へ送ったメッセージは、Email Sending のトラフィックとして数えられるよ
- Activity log と Email Sending のアナリティクスに表示されて、Email Routing のアナリティクスには出なくなるよ
- message.delivered や message.bounced などの Email Sending イベントが、イベントサブスクリプションに発行されるよ
- GraphQL Analytics API では、Email Sending のデータセットを新しい isVerifiedRecipient フィールドで絞り込めるよ

Email Routing だけを設定しているドメインから送るメッセージは、これまでどおりだよ。

## まとめ

- Email Sending が Workers Free プランで使えるようになったよ
- 認証済み宛先への送信は全プランで無料で、クォータにも数えられないよ
- 任意の宛先に送るには Workers Paid プランが必要だよ
- 認証済み送信の記録が、Email Routing から Email Sending に移ったよ

通知メールを、まず無料でさくっと試したい Workers 開発者のみんなに刺さるよ！

body_md_en:
Hi everyone, it's Shii-chan! Here's some happy news about trying things on the free tier!

## What was announced?

In the Cloudflare Changelog, Email Sending in Email Service became available on the Workers Free plan. It applies to sending to the verified destination addresses in your account.

## What changes

You can onboard sending domains without a paid plan. During development and testing you can send for free to verified destination addresses, then upgrade to the Workers Paid plan when going to production to send to arbitrary addresses. Use the Workers binding, the REST API, or SMTP to send alerts, reports, and notifications to your own team!

## Dive Deep

Sends to verified destination addresses are free on every plan. They do not count toward the monthly quota or the daily sending limits.

Here is a Workers binding example. Sending to an address that is not verified returns the error code E_RECIPIENT_PLAN_RESTRICTED.

```js
export default {
  async fetch(request, env) {
    try {
      await env.EMAIL.send({
        from: "alerts@yourdomain.com",
        to: "oncall@example.com", // A verified destination address
        subject: "Disk usage above 90%",
        text: "Disk usage on db-1 is above 90%.",
      });
    } catch (error) {
      if (error.code === "E_RECIPIENT_PLAN_RESTRICTED") {
        return new Response("Recipient is not a verified destination address", {
          status: 403,
        });
      }
      throw error;
    }
    return new Response("Alert sent");
  },
};
```

### How accounting changes

Before, sending to verified destination addresses was an Email Routing feature, and these messages were recorded as Email Routing traffic. This capability has now moved to Email Sending.

- Messages you send from a sending domain to verified destination addresses now count as Email Sending traffic
- They appear in the Activity log and Email Sending analytics, and no longer appear in Email Routing analytics
- Email Sending events such as message.delivered and message.bounced are published to your event subscriptions
- In the GraphQL Analytics API, filter the Email Sending datasets on the new isVerifiedRecipient field

Messages sent from a domain that has only Email Routing configured are unchanged.

## Wrap-up

- Email Sending is available on the Workers Free plan
- Sends to verified destination addresses are free on every plan and don't count toward quotas
- Sending to arbitrary recipients requires the Workers Paid plan
- Verified sends are now recorded under Email Sending instead of Email Routing

This is for Workers developers who want to try notification emails for free first!
